{
    "id": "kubevirt",
    "name": "KubeVirt",
    "tagline": "virtual machines as Kubernetes objects",
    "icon": "display",
    "docs": "https://kubevirt.io/user-guide/",
    "description": "KubeVirt runs virtual machines on Kubernetes as ordinary API objects: a VirtualMachine is the definition, a VirtualMachineInstance is the guest actually running, and it lives inside a virt-launcher pod on some node. Most of what this plugin lists is the machinery around that — the disks CDI imports, the live migrations, the instance types and preferences that let a VM be described by what it is rather than by how much RAM it wants.\n\nThe charts need a Prometheus, and read the kubevirt_vmi_* series virt-handler exports. Without one, everything else here still works and the chart panels say so. Metric names have moved between KubeVirt releases; if yours are different, copy this plugin into your own plugins folder under the same id and change the queries.\n\nGuest readings are not the same as pod readings, and that is the point of charting them separately: a VM's own CPU excludes the emulator threads its pod is charged for, and its memory is claimed up front in a way a container's is not. Where the two disagree, the guest chart is the one describing the machine somebody is logged into.",
    "requires": [
        {
            "kind": "crd:virtualmachines.kubevirt.io",
            "label": "Virtual Machines"
        },
        {
            "kind": "crd:virtualmachineinstances.kubevirt.io",
            "label": "Virtual Machine Instances"
        },
        {
            "kind": "crd:virtualmachineinstancemigrations.kubevirt.io",
            "label": "Migrations",
            "optional": true
        },
        {
            "kind": "crd:datavolumes.cdi.kubevirt.io",
            "label": "Data Volumes (CDI)",
            "optional": true
        },
        {
            "kind": "crd:network-attachment-definitions.k8s.cni.cncf.io",
            "label": "Networks (Multus)",
            "optional": true
        }
    ],
    "views": [
